WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.920
- Rumble Boxing is the group fitness class

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.040
that combines boxing
with strength training.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.700
Its popularity in the group fitness scene

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.800
has grown since it first
opened its doors in 2017,

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.320
and celebrities are taking notice.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.010
Walk into a Rumble class on any given day,

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.990
and you just might be
throwing a few punches

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.660
alongside Justin Bieber,
his wife, Hailey Bieber,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.400
maybe even David Beckham.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.640
Celebrities aren't just working out there.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.210
They're investing. Justin
Bieber and Rocky himself,

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:38.600
Sylvester Stallone,
have invested in Rumble.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.760
The New York-based workout
is growing rapidly,

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.830
with studio locations popping up all over,

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.740
from Philly to DC to LA to San Francisco.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.023
Noah: You know you're gonna get

00:00:50.023 --> 00:00:51.420
half the class on the bags,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.790
working traditional combinations,

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.910
getting your conditioning,
getting your cardio in,

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:58.660
and getting that all-empowering,
just, aggression out.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.320
And you know over here on these benches,

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.500
you're gonna get a strong weight workout.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.200
So you're gonna do your
squats, your lunges,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.760
your curls, your shoulder presses,

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.484
sprinkle in a little
burpees, all with, you know,

00:01:08.484 --> 00:01:09.540
under the red lights,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.820
under the black lights,
surrounded by a group

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.170
of just great, like-minded people

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.810
having fun and working hard.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.980
- The price of a Rumble
class is comparable

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.538
to other New York
boutique fitness studios,

00:01:19.538 --> 00:01:21.754
at $36 per class.

00:01:21.754 --> 00:01:23.200
But it could vary slightly

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.200
depending on which city you're in.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.710
And if a big class
isn't really your thing,

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:31.180
you can also choose to work
one-on-one with a Rumble trainer

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.320
to get more personalized attention.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.350
The individualized training of course

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.730
includes perfecting your boxing technique

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.480
plus working with weights.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.370
The private training sessions
in Manhattan start at $175,

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.510
a little higher than other boxing studios,

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.940
such as Overthrow or Shadowbox,

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.400
which start at around $120 per session.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.100
Regardless of price, people
clearly can't get enough

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.070
of Rumble, so my colleague
Kevin and I are going

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.870
to Rumble's Upper East Side
location here in New York City

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.420
to check out what the hype is all about.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.660
The class is 45 minutes and
is made up of 10 rounds,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.180
switching from the bag side to
the weight side continuously.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.690
It was nonstop movement!

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:15.130
If we weren't punching the
bag during the boxing rounds,

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.160
we were on the floor doing sit-ups.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.370
When we were watching the instructor

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.230
demonstrate the strength-training moves,

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.660
we were bouncing around to
keep our heart rates up.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.800
We started on the bags,
and by the time we got

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.900
to the weight section,
my muscles were on fire.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.610
But the lights, the music,
and the hyped-up instructor

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.780
definitely helped me push through.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.293
From there, we moved on

00:02:34.293 --> 00:02:36.620
to the private training session with Noah.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.480
This private training option is one

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.530
that celebs will often take.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.120
Noah went over the boxer stance
and the six boxing punches

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.330
for us, so we can perfect our form.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.140
We then did rounds of squats,

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.860
shoulder presses, and push-ups.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.420
As if our muscles weren't already tired,

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.090
we then threw punches on the bag.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.220
To say we were reaching
fatigue at this point

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.053
was an understatement.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.790
Kevin: I loved the class.
It was a lot of fun.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.240
It was big, high energy.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.590
It was fun to go in there
and hit the bags on one side

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:15.720
and then switch over to
the weights on the other.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.837
It was not like any other
class that I've been to,

00:03:17.837 --> 00:03:19.610
where most of the
classes are just directed

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:20.860
at one type of thing that you're gonna do

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.180
for the entire time.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.791
And it was fun to have the options of

00:03:23.791 --> 00:03:25.133
going back and forth on this.

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.165
Fabiana: I loved the high energy

00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:28.340
from the trainers, the
energy all around the room.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.173
The music was great.

00:03:29.173 --> 00:03:31.660
It was just, like, super motivating.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:32.680
Kevin: Even though it was really dark,

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:35.210
and it kind of closed you
off, I did find a lot of times

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:38.540
that I wasn't sure
exactly what I was doing

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.920
because of the lighting,
so I felt a little lost.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.020
But also that was a thing that allowed me

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.730
to not worry about what
was going on around me.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.640
I don't think it's
overpriced for that at all.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.770
Fabiana: Right, I totally agree.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.620
I think it's a fair price.
It's not astronomically higher

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.680
than other places, and you're
like, what am I getting

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.810
for that money?
Kevin: And you're gonna

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.190
spend the same kind of money

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.250
if you're going out for a few drinks

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.040
in Manhattan, so.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:03:59.873
Fabiana: There's something to say

00:03:59.873 --> 00:04:01.173
about the energy of a class

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:02.820
and just having all
those people around you,

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.895
and just the whole
experience of a Rumble class.

